UI/API	Loading/error/success states; all visible buttons work; mutations refresh from backend; production build succeeds.

Example seeded scenario
Input	Value
Batch	180 meals
Original safe-use window	75 minutes from scenario start
Rider capacities	Five riders with 40-meal capacity each
Initial shelter demand	Shelter A requests 50 meals; other shelters have separately configured needs and requirements.
Expected dispatch behavior	No rider exceeds capacity; no shelter exceeds demand; unallocated quantity remains explicitly accounted for.
Failure	A destination closes or reaches zero demand during transit.
Expected recovery	Revalidate feasible alternatives; reroute only if safe and capacity/demand allow; otherwise intervention alert.
Important	Do not hard-code an expected total delivery quantity without defining all shelter demands, travel times, safety margin, and other constraints.

Benchmark methodology
Compare baseline matching and Rescue Protocol on identical deterministic seeded scenarios. Measure safely delivered quantity, successful recovery rate, time to recovery, safety violations, and stock-accounting errors. Record the number of scenarios and exact configuration. Label all results as simulated. Do not claim a percentage improvement unless measured.
