•	Do not commit .env files, API keys, node_modules, build output, local secrets, or private operational data.
•	Verify the remote URL and branch before pushing. Do not force-push.
•	Keep README accurate about what is simulated and what is implemented.
•	Confirm repository access and the project submission URL before the deadline.
•	The problem statement explicitly asks for regular continuous commits during the sprint; avoid a single final dump.
Suggested repository description
AidFlow is a failure-resilient micro-logistics prototype for perishable surplus and emergency aid, with capacity-aware dispatch, reservation leases, cargo-aware recovery, and auditable safety constraints.
Suggested short project description
AidFlow coordinates surplus food and emergency aid between donors, volunteer riders, and shelters. Its Rescue Protocol evaluates fallback destinations, revalidates changing demand and resource constraints, and safely recovers failed assignments while preserving cargo and quantity accounting. A deterministic simulation lab lets judges reproduce ghost reservations, shelter closures, expiry risks, and recovery decisions.
17. Risks, Mitigations, and Honest Claims
Risk	Mitigation
Scope exceeds six hours	Freeze P0 scope; cut map polish, AI, and advanced routing first.
Agent writes impressive but untested code	Require test output, run the app, inspect diff, verify all visible controls.
Race condition or double allocation	Use transactions/constraints, idempotent operations, and concurrency/duplicate-request tests.
Incorrect food/medical assumptions	Use configured rules supplied by operator/authoritative policy; do not invent universal safety limits.
In-transit cargo mishandled	Separate cargo custody from assignment state; require explicit handover.
False impact claim	Report only measured simulation results with scenario count and configuration.
Map/API fails during judging	Use a local schematic and simulated ETA, clearly labeled.
Demo clock makes time tests flaky	Use an injectable simulation clock and deterministic seed data.
Over-designed UI slows operation	Keep one primary action per state, explain disabled actions, prioritize Rescue Queue.

Claims we can make if verified
•	The prototype enforces configured capacity, demand, compatibility, and deadline constraints.
•	The timeout processor releases an eligible reservation exactly once under tested conditions.
•	The recovery engine revalidates fallback destinations and preserves in-transit cargo accounting.
•	The simulation benchmark measured specified outcomes on documented seeded scenarios.
Claims to avoid without evidence
•	We eliminate food waste in real cities.
•	We reduce spoilage by a specific percentage in the real world.
•	We provide real-time traffic prediction or live GPS if using simulated values.
•	All food/medical deliveries are guaranteed safe.
•	The algorithm is globally unique or has no competitors.
